WEBVTT

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:07.570
Out!

00:00:07.850 --> 00:00:10.440
First set winner: Maruo.

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:12.190
Score: 6-2.

00:00:12.190 --> 00:00:13.640
I can't believe it!

00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:15.160
Maruo won a set!

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:17.110
<i>This is where...</i>

00:00:18.490 --> 00:00:20.970
<i>This is where the real match starts!</i>

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:56.970
Awakening to Simplicity

00:01:57.430 --> 00:01:58.630
Second set!

00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:01.560
<i>His play style is different now.</i>

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:02.860
<i>I have to find a way to deal</i>

00:02:02.860 --> 00:02:05.050
<i>with nine different serves 
without relying on my data.</i>

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:10.100
<i>That toss looks like it's going to be a spin.</i>

00:02:10.390 --> 00:02:12.030
<i>Will he go with his best shot?</i>

00:02:12.030 --> 00:02:12.980
<i>Or will he switch?</i>

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:17.630
15-love.

00:02:17.630 --> 00:02:19.200
<i>It spun forward!</i>

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:21.070
<i>His delivery hasn't changed,</i>

00:02:21.070 --> 00:02:24.690
<i>but I'm a step behind because I keep 
focusing on all the possibilities.</i>

00:02:25.330 --> 00:02:27.930
<i>Isn't there anything</i>

00:02:27.930 --> 00:02:29.830
<i>that can help me narrow down his options?</i>

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:32.620
<i>A center spin!</i>

00:02:32.620 --> 00:02:34.790
<i>Does that mean he's gonna move up?!</i>

00:02:36.520 --> 00:02:37.760
30-love.

00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:39.220
<i>It's no use.</i>

00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:41.480
<i>Even if I'm aware of it, I'm 
still a step behind on his serve,</i>

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:42.900
<i>so my return is weaker.</i>

00:02:45.110 --> 00:02:46.140
40-love.

00:02:46.890 --> 00:02:48.920
<i>He went with his classic wide slice!</i>

00:02:50.250 --> 00:02:51.400
<i>Keep calm...</i>

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:53.890
<i>The side returning the serve 
is always at a disadvantage.</i>

00:02:53.890 --> 00:02:56.050
<i>I'm just gonna have to gamble a bit.</i>

00:02:56.710 --> 00:02:59.800
<i>If I keep an eye out for his 
strongest wide flat serve,</i>

00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:02.530
<i>I might be able to handle it, even if I'm wrong.</i>

00:03:03.070 --> 00:03:04.070
<i>Wide slice!</i>

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:06.240
<i>He's going to use his backhand!</i>

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:07.160
<i>Will it go down the line?</i>

00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:08.160
<i>Or crosscourt?!</i>

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:12.670
<i>His backhand finally made it in!</i>

00:03:12.990 --> 00:03:15.380
Game: Alex. 1-0.

00:03:16.370 --> 00:03:19.640
<i>But Alex isn't used to playing like this.</i>

00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:21.180
<i>Even if he's started to make shots...</i>

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:24.690
<i>I shouldn't change my plan 
to go after his backhand!</i>

00:03:25.850 --> 00:03:26.800
Huh?

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:28.680
Alex and Eichiro?

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:32.140
Hey, Atsushi, what's the score?

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:36.070
Maruo won the first set and 
they're in their second set, 3-all.

00:03:36.070 --> 00:03:38.680
Why is Alex losing?!

00:03:38.680 --> 00:03:41.150
He missed a lot of backhands.

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:44.530
But he started making his 
backhands in the second set,

00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:46.660
and he's been in the lead since then.

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:48.810
Maruo is struggling to keep his lead,

00:03:48.810 --> 00:03:51.320
but Alex is keeping the pressure on him.

00:03:52.260 --> 00:03:54.750
Game: Alex. 4-3.

00:04:00.060 --> 00:04:03.090
<i>Alex will definitely go for the break.</i>

00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:06.710
<i>But I know the characteristics of his backhand now!</i>

00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:11.140
Alex's Backhand
Cross= Fast prep          Line= Slow prep

00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:11.140
Setup is 
ready here

00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:11.140
Setup isn't 
ready here yet

00:04:06.710 --> 00:04:09.090
<i>His prep is fast when he's aiming to hit crosscourt.</i>

00:04:09.090 --> 00:04:11.140
<i>When his prep is slow, he's aiming down the line.</i>

00:04:11.530 --> 00:04:13.430
<i>If I can just hold serve by using this data,</i>

00:04:13.430 --> 00:04:14.900
<i>I can change the tide!</i>

00:04:15.190 --> 00:04:16.020
Time!

00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:18.520
Alex?

00:04:20.950 --> 00:04:22.530
<i>He's smiling.</i>

00:04:22.930 --> 00:04:25.310
<i>I'll target all my serves at his backhand.</i>

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:30.160
<i>I'll hit this to his backhand, too!</i>

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:33.280
<i>Keep targeting his backhand with a
delivery strong enough to win the point.</i>

00:04:33.280 --> 00:04:37.460
<i>That way, Alex's stance will move more 
and more toward his backhand side.</i>

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:40.500
<i>Once he's more than a meter 
back from the center line,</i>

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:42.920
<i>hit hard to his forehand!</i>

00:04:43.220 --> 00:04:44.520
<i>Even if he's better with his forehand,</i>

00:04:44.520 --> 00:04:46.740
<i>he won't have enough strength to 
hit it hard while he's running.</i>

00:04:47.550 --> 00:04:48.950
<i>At his backhand again!</i>

00:04:49.800 --> 00:04:53.430
<i>Alex's backhand delivery is losing 
its stability and strength.</i>

00:04:53.740 --> 00:04:56.440
<i>If I can't hit a sure shot from back here, then...</i>

00:04:56.440 --> 00:04:57.350
<i>I will from at the net!</i>

00:04:58.320 --> 00:04:59.930
<i>If his prep is fast, then it's crosscourt!</i>

00:04:59.930 --> 00:05:01.480
<i>If it's slow, it's down the line!</i>

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:03.180
<i>Bring it!</i>

00:05:03.180 --> 00:05:03.990
<i>Which is it?</i>

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:08.160
<i>What?!</i>

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:18.170
Love-15.

00:05:18.170 --> 00:05:20.290
<i>He pivoted into his forehand.</i>

00:05:20.290 --> 00:05:23.130
<i>Here... With that timing...</i>

00:05:23.570 --> 00:05:24.900
<i>That's it!</i>

00:05:24.900 --> 00:05:28.260
<i>An offensive backhand maximizes 
my forehand's effectiveness.</i>

00:05:28.570 --> 00:05:31.280
<i>But as long as it's his backhand, 
I can see where the ball will go.</i>

00:05:31.280 --> 00:05:33.770
<i>I'll just have to wait for a chance 
while targeting his backhand.</i>

00:05:33.770 --> 00:05:35.140
<i>If his prep is slow, it's down the line!</i>

00:05:35.760 --> 00:05:36.640
<i>Even if I can read it, it's tough.</i>

00:05:38.210 --> 00:05:41.640
<i>If my backhand gets better, 
I'll surpass the player I was,</i>

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:43.530
<i>who relied only on his forehand!</i>

00:05:44.500 --> 00:05:46.050
Love-30.

00:05:46.050 --> 00:05:47.100
Amazing!

00:05:47.100 --> 00:05:48.500
Good shot, Alex!

00:05:48.500 --> 00:05:51.740
If the ball is even a little weak, 
he goes for it with a strong forehand.

00:05:52.010 --> 00:05:56.250
<i>So he's still gonna go with 
his forehand in the end.</i>

00:05:56.250 --> 00:05:57.120
<i>How stubborn.</i>

00:05:57.510 --> 00:06:01.030
<i>Then I'll make his backhand difficult to hit, too!</i>

00:06:02.610 --> 00:06:04.050
<i>Be more relentless!</i>

00:06:04.940 --> 00:06:06.800
Out! Love-40.

00:06:07.130 --> 00:06:09.890
<i>This is bad. It's break point.</i>

00:06:09.890 --> 00:06:11.790
<i>No, don't lose heart now.</i>

00:06:11.790 --> 00:06:14.650
<i>Keep an eye out for his forehand and 
don't let your shots get weaker!</i>

00:06:14.650 --> 00:06:15.390
<i>At his backhand!</i>

00:06:16.730 --> 00:06:17.230
<i>Huh?!</i>

00:06:19.870 --> 00:06:21.090
<i>He got me.</i>

00:06:21.090 --> 00:06:23.440
<i>He ran around to his forehand 
during the return...</i>

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:26.320
Game: Alex. 5-3.

00:06:26.610 --> 00:06:27.950
That's a pro for you.

00:06:27.950 --> 00:06:31.060
Even if he figured out the serves 
were targeting his backhand,

00:06:31.060 --> 00:06:32.930
that forehand was more impressive than usual.

00:06:32.930 --> 00:06:34.580
Yeah. He has a chance.

00:06:34.820 --> 00:06:37.960
<i>It's been a while since I've felt this way.</i>

00:06:38.390 --> 00:06:40.120
<i>He broke my serve.</i>

00:06:40.120 --> 00:06:43.650
<i>He'll take the set if I don't break his serve now.</i>

00:06:43.650 --> 00:06:44.800
<i>What do I do?</i>

00:06:44.800 --> 00:06:46.870
<i>Just solidifying my defense isn't enough.</i>

00:06:46.870 --> 00:06:48.470
<i>But how do I go after him?</i>

00:06:48.470 --> 00:06:50.660
Maruo, are you ready?

00:06:50.660 --> 00:06:52.220
What?! Uh, yeah!

00:06:52.900 --> 00:06:54.550
<i>I can't think of anything!</i>

00:06:55.030 --> 00:06:55.720
<i>Then...</i>

00:06:56.060 --> 00:06:57.920
<i>Keep the strategy simple.</i>

00:06:57.920 --> 00:06:59.540
<i>I'll make it hard for him 
to use his forehand.</i>

00:06:59.540 --> 00:07:00.730
<i>That's all.</i>

00:07:00.730 --> 00:07:02.100
<i>Forget the Alex who's in my data.</i>

00:07:02.100 --> 00:07:03.710
<i>Watch the Alex who's in front of me!</i>

00:07:03.710 --> 00:07:05.860
<i>Keep my eyes on him, 
and the rest is up to chance!</i>

00:07:09.080 --> 00:07:10.280
<i>It's on the line.</i>

00:07:10.280 --> 00:07:11.160
<i>Then...</i>

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:12.230
<i>Crosscourt!</i>

00:07:12.780 --> 00:07:13.610
<i>It's in.</i>

00:07:13.610 --> 00:07:14.730
<i>But it'll come back.</i>

00:07:14.730 --> 00:07:17.050
<i>And I'll decide where this ball goes</i>

00:07:17.050 --> 00:07:19.040
<i>when I hit it!</i>

00:07:19.830 --> 00:07:20.710
<i>It's deep...</i>

00:07:24.150 --> 00:07:25.390
He's moving up!

00:07:25.390 --> 00:07:26.300
That's good.

00:07:26.850 --> 00:07:27.800
<i>Huh?!</i>

00:07:29.730 --> 00:07:31.170
Love-15.

00:07:32.450 --> 00:07:34.300
<i>Did his delivery get a little better?</i>

00:07:34.700 --> 00:07:35.840
<i>Why?</i>

00:07:35.840 --> 00:07:38.680
<i>Why did I just move up?</i>

00:07:39.290 --> 00:07:40.360
<i>This is tough.</i>

00:07:40.800 --> 00:07:43.350
<i>But I'm returning far more 
than I did in the last game.</i>

00:07:43.560 --> 00:07:46.700
Hey, did their rally just get a lot better?

00:07:46.700 --> 00:07:48.360
Yeah, it did.

00:07:54.900 --> 00:07:56.950
<i>What is this?</i>

00:08:01.460 --> 00:08:04.960
<i>It's like my body is reacting before 
I have a chance to think about it.</i>

00:08:09.270 --> 00:08:10.460
Love-30.

00:08:10.950 --> 00:08:13.970
<i>A great hit went in the ideal path,</i>

00:08:14.730 --> 00:08:18.640
<i>even though I decided to aim 
there at the last second.</i>

00:08:19.420 --> 00:08:24.890
<i>That's the best I've ever been able to 
actualize the control I've been practicing.</i>

00:08:24.890 --> 00:08:26.810
<i>If this isn't a coincidence,</i>

00:08:26.810 --> 00:08:30.280
<i>does it mean my body automatically 
moved to make the best decision?</i>

00:08:30.280 --> 00:08:34.490
<i>That short hit crosscourt was clearly 
the best option to take.</i>

00:08:34.490 --> 00:08:35.810
<i>Does that mean my body...</i>

00:08:35.810 --> 00:08:39.700
<i>My instincts are making more accurate 
judgments than I realized?</i>

00:08:40.660 --> 00:08:46.080
<i>It might be better to rely on my 
body than on my head right now.</i>

00:08:46.520 --> 00:08:48.840
<i>In any case, let's try that one more time.</i>

00:08:49.570 --> 00:08:51.590
<i>Maruo's movements have changed.</i>

00:08:51.590 --> 00:08:53.600
<i>I'm done using my head.</i>

00:08:53.600 --> 00:08:55.600
<i>Once we start, I free my mind!</i>

00:08:57.830 --> 00:08:59.630
15-30.

00:08:59.630 --> 00:09:00.860
<i>Wrong, wrong!</i>

00:09:00.860 --> 00:09:03.100
<i>How does being totally mindless help?!</i>

00:09:03.430 --> 00:09:04.570
<i>I need to look more</i>

00:09:04.570 --> 00:09:06.530
<i>at my opponent and the entirety of the court,</i>

00:09:06.530 --> 00:09:08.560
<i>and be aware of the Alex, 
right in front of me.</i>

00:09:08.560 --> 00:09:12.360
<i>Trust that my data, my instincts, 
will choose the right thing to do...</i>

00:09:13.360 --> 00:09:14.490
<i>And focus on the ball!</i>

00:09:22.680 --> 00:09:24.010
30-all.

00:09:24.010 --> 00:09:24.770
Yes!

00:09:24.770 --> 00:09:26.500
His serve and volley were both perfect!

00:09:26.730 --> 00:09:27.890
<i>He got me.</i>

00:09:27.890 --> 00:09:29.380
<i>But it's not a bad thing.</i>

00:09:29.780 --> 00:09:31.430
<i>After we started this set,</i>

00:09:31.430 --> 00:09:33.910
<i>he finally started returning 
my serves decently.</i>

00:09:33.910 --> 00:09:36.760
<i>I knew it. Something's changed within this game.</i>

00:09:37.240 --> 00:09:39.010
<i>I might be able to do it!</i>

00:09:39.440 --> 00:09:42.290
<i>The score is 5-3, and I'm in the lead.</i>

00:09:42.290 --> 00:09:44.280
<i>But if I stumble now, I'm in trouble.</i>

00:09:44.280 --> 00:09:46.020
<i>I can sense it.</i>

00:09:46.920 --> 00:09:50.400
<i>This is the same sensation as having 
your livelihood depend on each match.</i>

00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:52.240
<i>Something being a pro has taught me.</i>

00:09:52.770 --> 00:09:54.180
<i>It's something I have</i>

00:09:54.180 --> 00:09:55.530
<i>that Maruo doesn't!</i>

00:09:57.030 --> 00:09:58.740
40-30.

00:09:58.740 --> 00:10:01.530
Count on a pro to be able to 
win points at times like this.

00:10:02.460 --> 00:10:04.130
<i>I'm reacting fine.</i>

00:10:04.130 --> 00:10:06.410
<i>I just need to return that serve.</i>

00:10:06.980 --> 00:10:08.790
<i>Thinking stops now.</i>

00:10:08.790 --> 00:10:11.500
<i>Just be aware of Alex and 
the entirety of the court,</i>

00:10:11.500 --> 00:10:14.040
<i>and rely on my instincts in the moment!</i>

00:10:14.500 --> 00:10:17.240
<i>Believe in myself! I've gotten this far!</i>

00:10:20.780 --> 00:10:22.800
<i>He returned that solid serve perfectly!</i>

00:10:28.690 --> 00:10:30.690
What an angle!

00:10:30.690 --> 00:10:33.070
<i>My backhand is already my weapon!</i>

00:10:33.070 --> 00:10:34.070
<i>Down the line!</i>

00:10:37.190 --> 00:10:39.750
Second set winner: Alex.

00:10:39.750 --> 00:10:41.450
Score: 6-3.

00:10:41.720 --> 00:10:42.950
Yes!

00:10:42.950 --> 00:10:45.970
<i>I knew it, but I still couldn't hit it...</i>

00:10:47.050 --> 00:10:48.310
<i>Amazing!</i>

00:10:48.310 --> 00:10:51.860
<i>I'm playing an amazing match 
against an amazing player!</i>

00:10:53.350 --> 00:10:57.370
<i>I used to think Maruo was the insecure type 
who isn't capable of having big dreams.</i>

00:10:57.370 --> 00:10:58.420
<i>But that's not right.</i>

00:10:58.890 --> 00:11:01.570
<i>He's the type to have countless smaller dreams</i>

00:11:01.570 --> 00:11:03.890
<i>that he can achieve perfectly, one by one.</i>

00:11:04.330 --> 00:11:06.190
<i>They may be small individually,</i>

00:11:06.190 --> 00:11:09.600
<i>but as they keep coming true, 
they quickly become one huge dream.</i>

00:11:10.010 --> 00:11:11.280
<i>I'll prioritize this one point</i>

00:11:11.280 --> 00:11:14.120
<i>in front of me instead of 
thinking about the future.</i>

00:11:14.120 --> 00:11:16.040
<i>This is way a pro thinks.</i>

00:11:16.040 --> 00:11:19.610
<i>If I've come this far in just a 
year and a half by doing that,</i>

00:11:19.610 --> 00:11:21.860
<i>then as a professional, I can't lose.</i>

00:11:24.880 --> 00:11:26.070
<i>I'm doing it.</i>

00:11:26.070 --> 00:11:28.420
<i>I'm holding my own against a pro!</i>

00:11:28.420 --> 00:11:30.510
<i>I could very well win!</i>

00:11:31.030 --> 00:11:32.170
Time.

00:11:37.590 --> 00:11:39.170
Final set.

00:11:39.170 --> 00:11:40.790
<i>Even if I can read his backhand,</i>

00:11:40.790 --> 00:11:42.520
<i>I can't return the ball.</i>

00:11:42.520 --> 00:11:45.240
<i>It's dangerous to keep 
aiming there so blatantly.</i>

00:11:45.240 --> 00:11:46.640
<i>So what do I do?</i>

00:11:47.220 --> 00:11:48.800
<i>I have to stop thinking.</i>

00:11:48.800 --> 00:11:50.870
<i>The rest is up to what he does.</i>

00:11:50.870 --> 00:11:52.560
<i>Believe in myself...</i>

00:11:53.240 --> 00:11:54.560
<i>and trust my instincts!</i>

00:11:55.060 --> 00:11:58.320
<i>I'll challenge you with my 
clearly superior strength here!</i>

00:11:58.610 --> 00:11:59.740
<i>He's pushing forward!</i>

00:12:00.570 --> 00:12:01.240
<i>Hard hit!</i>

00:12:01.880 --> 00:12:03.240
<i>But it dropped in time!</i>

00:12:04.260 --> 00:12:05.220
<i>Where do I aim?</i>

00:12:05.220 --> 00:12:05.840
<i>Up?</i>

00:12:05.840 --> 00:12:06.420
<i>Right?</i>

00:12:06.420 --> 00:12:07.200
<i>Left?</i>

00:12:07.200 --> 00:12:09.390
<i>A return is risky, but I'm ready for it!</i>

00:12:09.390 --> 00:12:10.450
<i>What will you do?</i>

00:12:10.700 --> 00:12:12.960
<i>Look at your opponent to 
determine where to aim...</i>

00:12:14.750 --> 00:12:15.400
Yes!

00:12:15.400 --> 00:12:16.710
15-love.

00:12:17.730 --> 00:12:18.840
<i>I can't read him.</i>

00:12:19.290 --> 00:12:22.260
<i>If I can just play like that, 
he'll never be able to read me.</i>

00:12:22.260 --> 00:12:24.840
<i>Even I don't know where I'll 
aim until the last moment.</i>

00:12:25.460 --> 00:12:28.240
There's not a lot of power to it, 
but it follows the course.

00:12:28.240 --> 00:12:29.640
Is he doing it on purpose?

00:12:29.640 --> 00:12:31.180
He probably is.

00:12:31.430 --> 00:12:34.660
<i>Boldly rushing forward is a pattern I can use.</i>

00:12:34.660 --> 00:12:37.560
<i>All right, I'm starting to understand it.</i>

00:12:37.560 --> 00:12:49.240
Reason

00:12:37.560 --> 00:12:49.240
Instinct

00:12:37.780 --> 00:12:43.450
<i>My instincts have been listening 
to my reasoning all along.</i>

00:12:43.450 --> 00:12:46.550
<i>So I can move the right way during play...</i>

00:12:47.570 --> 00:12:49.240
<i>I'm counting on you, instincts!</i>

00:12:53.580 --> 00:12:55.740
Game: Maruo. 3-2.

00:13:00.410 --> 00:13:02.730
Well, see you later, Maruo-kun.

00:13:04.470 --> 00:13:06.840
Game: Alex. 4-all.

00:13:06.840 --> 00:13:08.980
Maruo with his control,

00:13:08.980 --> 00:13:11.730
and Alex with his intense serve and stroke.

00:13:11.730 --> 00:13:13.710
They're both counters to one another.

00:13:13.710 --> 00:13:15.640
Neither of them can break.

00:13:17.900 --> 00:13:20.150
Game: Alex. 6-all.

00:13:20.150 --> 00:13:21.890
We're finally at a tiebreaker.

00:13:22.500 --> 00:13:25.280
I didn't realize how much 
better Eichiro has gotten...

00:13:25.280 --> 00:13:27.410
<i>He isn't losing strength at all.</i>

00:13:27.410 --> 00:13:28.850
<i>If anything, he's getting stronger!</i>

00:13:28.850 --> 00:13:30.820
<i>No, don't hesitate now.</i>

00:13:30.820 --> 00:13:31.930
<i>It starts here.</i>

00:13:31.930 --> 00:13:33.790
<i>I have to get seven points first!</i>

00:13:36.010 --> 00:13:37.470
1-0: Maruo.

00:13:38.280 --> 00:13:39.450
1-all.

00:13:40.680 --> 00:13:42.550
2-1: Alex.

00:13:42.550 --> 00:13:44.430
3-2: Maruo.

00:13:44.430 --> 00:13:46.680
Both of them are holding serve.

00:13:47.110 --> 00:13:48.330
5-all.

00:13:53.750 --> 00:13:55.930
6-5: Alex.

00:13:55.930 --> 00:13:56.850
Here it is!

00:13:56.850 --> 00:13:59.040
Match point for Alex!

00:13:59.040 --> 00:14:02.300
But if Maruo can hold his next two serves,

00:14:02.300 --> 00:14:04.360
he'll get to match point instead.

00:14:04.360 --> 00:14:06.440
The situation is a complete tie.

00:14:06.860 --> 00:14:10.330
By now, both of them must 
be pretty spent physically.

00:14:10.330 --> 00:14:13.660
How well can Maruo stay calm 
and use his control?

00:14:14.090 --> 00:14:16.810
Will Alex push relentlessly with power?

00:14:16.810 --> 00:14:19.710
In the end, it's a battle of wills.

00:14:19.710 --> 00:14:22.000
<i>I've come this far. I won't lose!</i>

00:14:22.390 --> 00:14:24.050
<i>I'll end it here.</i>

00:14:24.050 --> 00:14:24.880
<i>Bring it!</i>

00:14:27.130 --> 00:14:28.760
A slow ball to his forehand?!

00:14:30.490 --> 00:14:31.850
<i>His timing was off!</i>

00:14:31.850 --> 00:14:32.510
<i>I can do it!</i>

00:14:35.410 --> 00:14:36.850
What incredible control!

00:14:37.240 --> 00:14:38.480
6-all.

00:14:39.600 --> 00:14:40.910
All right!

00:14:40.910 --> 00:14:42.370
He staved off match point!

00:14:42.370 --> 00:14:43.820
It's still gonna go on?

00:14:44.030 --> 00:14:48.490
Alex intended to stop a fast serve 
from Maruo with his forehand.

00:14:48.490 --> 00:14:52.200
But then Maruo used a slow slice 
that made Alex miss his timing.

00:14:52.200 --> 00:14:56.350
While Alex was caught up in the match, 
Maruo found his blind spot.

00:14:56.350 --> 00:15:00.830
Even in this situation, Maruo 
is making rational decisions.

00:15:00.830 --> 00:15:03.920
<i>This is the best tennis I've ever played.</i>

00:15:03.920 --> 00:15:06.210
<i>If I don't win now, then when?!</i>

00:15:06.500 --> 00:15:07.910
Final set.

00:15:07.910 --> 00:15:10.000
6-all in the tiebreaker.

00:15:10.000 --> 00:15:13.610
From this point on, whoever 
gets two points ahead wins.

00:15:13.610 --> 00:15:15.830
Even a pro would get 
nervous in this situation.

00:15:15.830 --> 00:15:17.470
Is Maruo okay?

00:15:19.850 --> 00:15:21.080
The serve's fast this time!

00:15:21.080 --> 00:15:23.160
Alex misread the timing.

00:15:25.330 --> 00:15:26.950
7-6: Maruo.

00:15:27.650 --> 00:15:29.990
Now it's match point for Maruo.

00:15:30.810 --> 00:15:31.990
Alex...

00:15:32.370 --> 00:15:34.490
<i>If I get this next one, I'll win!</i>

00:15:37.420 --> 00:15:38.020
<i>Huh?</i>

00:15:39.220 --> 00:15:40.180
<i>Ow!</i>

00:15:40.180 --> 00:15:41.750
<i>No... Don't tell me...</i>

00:15:43.300 --> 00:15:44.870
<i>A leg cramp?!</i>

00:15:46.000 --> 00:15:48.640
<i>I come this far and then get a leg cramp?!</i>

00:15:48.640 --> 00:15:51.190
<i>All this time, I thought Alex 
and I were evenly matched.</i>

00:15:51.190 --> 00:15:53.430
<i>Was my body actually pushing too hard?</i>

00:15:53.670 --> 00:15:55.530
<i>I-It hurts...</i>

00:15:55.530 --> 00:15:59.690
<i>But if I tell the coach, he'll stop the match.</i>

00:15:59.690 --> 00:16:02.560
<i>Stopping at match point?
You've got to be kidding me!</i>

00:16:02.560 --> 00:16:03.610
<i>What do I do?</i>

00:16:03.610 --> 00:16:05.440
<i>If I move, it'll be obvious.</i>

00:16:05.440 --> 00:16:07.830
<i>Which means I'll have to win
the point the moment it starts.</i>

00:16:07.830 --> 00:16:09.530
<i>That means a return ace.</i>

00:16:09.530 --> 00:16:10.970
<i>It hurts like crazy,</i>

00:16:10.970 --> 00:16:13.820
<i>but I'll deal with it for a second, 
stand as firm as I can,</i>

00:16:14.170 --> 00:16:15.820
<i>and make it in one shot!</i>

00:16:15.820 --> 00:16:17.580
<i>Probably down the center!</i>

00:16:17.580 --> 00:16:19.040
<i>Here it comes! Please, I beg of you...</i>

00:16:20.700 --> 00:16:22.200
<i>Go in!</i>

00:16:26.520 --> 00:16:27.590
It hit the frame!

00:16:28.090 --> 00:16:29.100
It's coming back!

00:16:30.200 --> 00:16:30.890
Huh?

00:16:30.890 --> 00:16:32.770
There's something wrong 
with how Maruo's moving!

00:16:36.810 --> 00:16:38.470
<i>There's practically no chance of winning.</i>

00:16:38.470 --> 00:16:41.540
<i>But being at the net raises my chances, 
even if only by one percent!</i>

00:16:41.540 --> 00:16:43.660
<i>You hurt your leg and gambled, huh?</i>

00:16:43.660 --> 00:16:44.570
<i>Well, then!</i>

00:17:21.690 --> 00:17:22.890
<i>Out?</i>

00:17:22.890 --> 00:17:23.950
<i>That means...</i>

00:17:23.950 --> 00:17:24.810
<i>I win—</i>

00:17:24.810 --> 00:17:25.770
Idiot!

00:17:26.640 --> 00:17:28.080
Uh, I'm okay.

00:17:28.080 --> 00:17:29.550
It's just a cramp.

00:17:29.550 --> 00:17:31.270
That's not for you to say!

00:17:31.660 --> 00:17:33.690
As the coach, that's for me to decide.

00:17:33.690 --> 00:17:35.320
Y-Yes, sir.

00:17:35.320 --> 00:17:38.660
If you have goals, don't put 
your body through this again.

00:17:39.860 --> 00:17:41.160
Goals...

00:17:42.230 --> 00:17:44.410
<i>The All-Japan Junior.</i>

00:17:45.850 --> 00:17:47.210
I'm sorry.

00:17:47.210 --> 00:17:49.790
Atsushi, take Maruo to the medical office.

00:17:53.830 --> 00:17:55.220
Alex...

00:17:55.220 --> 00:17:58.050
I  never thought I'd lose to this amateur.

00:17:58.050 --> 00:17:59.790
I-I'm sorry.

00:17:59.790 --> 00:18:02.370
That last part was really a fluke.

00:18:02.370 --> 00:18:07.070
But I didn't want to lose or 
stop the match partway.

00:18:07.070 --> 00:18:10.530
Maruo, in this match, you taught me something.

00:18:11.990 --> 00:18:14.570
How important it is to look back at the past.

00:18:14.980 --> 00:18:15.710
Huh?

00:18:16.840 --> 00:18:18.930
To change the person I am right now,

00:18:18.930 --> 00:18:21.550
it's necessary to face the person I used to be.

00:18:22.710 --> 00:18:26.330
I was able to move a step forward today.

00:18:26.980 --> 00:18:32.840
But a match like this is meant to be 
played in front of a big audience.

00:18:38.040 --> 00:18:38.710
Yeah.

00:18:39.970 --> 00:18:43.030
Game, set. Winner: Maruo.

00:18:43.940 --> 00:18:46.310
<i>I won.</i>

00:18:46.960 --> 00:18:48.400
<i>Against a pro like Alex.</i>

00:18:50.480 --> 00:18:52.730
Florida Exchange Program Last Day

00:18:53.150 --> 00:18:58.490
Uh, everyone, thank you for the last two weeks.

00:18:59.080 --> 00:19:02.280
Especially Atsushi-san. Thanks for all your help.

00:19:02.280 --> 00:19:03.650
Don't mention it.

00:19:03.650 --> 00:19:06.240
Give me a call the next time 
you come around, okay?

00:19:06.530 --> 00:19:08.990
I'm really glad we met.

00:19:08.990 --> 00:19:11.380
It was fun, and I had a great time.

00:19:12.550 --> 00:19:14.000
Right, Alex?

00:19:14.000 --> 00:19:16.910
Maybe if I'd hit it from the side instead 
of a lob, I would've made it in.

00:19:16.910 --> 00:19:19.610
His loss yesterday is just now hitting him.

00:19:16.910 --> 00:19:22.510
No, I wouldn't have made that decision 
if I'd based it on Maruo's condition.

00:19:19.610 --> 00:19:22.510
Where's the friendly, 
relaxed Alex from yesterday?

00:19:22.860 --> 00:19:24.070
But that aside...

00:19:27.500 --> 00:19:30.830
That was an incredible match 
that I'll never forget.

00:19:31.450 --> 00:19:34.520
I'm hoping to get my revenge 
in a future match against you.

00:19:35.940 --> 00:19:37.400
Alex...

00:19:40.860 --> 00:19:43.270
You helped me out a lot, too.

00:19:43.270 --> 00:19:45.110
Thanks, Marcia.

00:19:45.110 --> 00:19:48.520
I never thought you'd beat my brother.

00:19:48.520 --> 00:19:49.290
Huh?

00:19:49.290 --> 00:19:52.550
But since you won, you'd better go pro.

00:19:52.550 --> 00:19:54.040
I will, too.

00:19:55.640 --> 00:19:58.420
<i>Y-You're rooting for me, right?</i>

00:19:58.420 --> 00:20:00.660
Th-Thanks, Marcia.

00:20:03.130 --> 00:20:06.310
Mike, do you know where Ike-kun is?

00:20:06.310 --> 00:20:09.030
I was able to play a lot 
of matches because of him.

00:20:09.030 --> 00:20:11.330
I'd like to thank him.

00:20:11.330 --> 00:20:14.010
He's been away at a match since yesterday.

00:20:14.010 --> 00:20:17.070
Speaking of, he left a message for you.

00:20:17.070 --> 00:20:20.100
He said, "If you want to thank 
someone, thank Natsu."

00:20:20.100 --> 00:20:22.090
Why Nat-chan?

00:20:22.090 --> 00:20:23.070
Who knows?

00:20:23.920 --> 00:20:26.070
Okay, I just push this, right?

00:20:26.070 --> 00:20:28.660
I'd like to get a picture with everyone together.

00:20:28.660 --> 00:20:30.630
Ready? Here goes.

00:20:32.280 --> 00:20:34.170
Bye, everyone!

00:20:34.170 --> 00:20:35.460
Let's meet again!

00:20:35.460 --> 00:20:36.900
Keep working hard!

00:20:36.900 --> 00:20:38.260
Take care of yourself.

00:20:38.260 --> 00:20:39.630
See you!

00:20:39.630 --> 00:20:40.810
See you.

00:20:49.970 --> 00:20:52.430
<i>It's been a productive two weeks.</i>

00:20:53.010 --> 00:20:54.810
<i>I was able to play a match with Ike-kun,</i>

00:20:54.810 --> 00:20:56.720
<i>and I even won in the end against Alex,</i>

00:20:56.720 --> 00:20:58.640
<i>who destroyed me in the beginning.</i>

00:20:59.110 --> 00:21:01.320
<i>On top of gaining two weeks' worth of data,</i>

00:21:01.320 --> 00:21:04.410
<i>my reason and instincts started 
to mesh surprisingly well.</i>

00:21:05.050 --> 00:21:08.870
<i>It'll be pretty difficult to get 
into that condition again.</i>

00:21:09.910 --> 00:21:12.110
<i>It was a miracle of a win, but...</i>

00:21:12.110 --> 00:21:13.580
<i>I still won.</i>

00:21:14.770 --> 00:21:17.350
<i>I have to connect this win to my next.</i>

00:21:18.260 --> 00:21:19.130
What is this?

00:21:19.130 --> 00:21:43.300
1 win, 1 loss.
We'll settle it next time!
Atsushi

00:21:19.800 --> 00:21:21.170
<i>When did they...</i>

00:21:21.630 --> 00:21:25.440
<i>"Next time, come visit with 
your girlfriend. Pedro."</i>

00:21:25.440 --> 00:21:27.970
<i>"Let's meet at Wimbledon. Robbie."</i>

00:21:28.520 --> 00:21:31.710
<i>"One win, one loss. We'll settle it next time."</i>

00:21:31.710 --> 00:21:33.360
<i>That's from Atsushi-san.</i>

00:21:33.360 --> 00:21:36.540
<i>"I won't lose anymore." That's Christopher.</i>

00:21:36.540 --> 00:21:39.540
<i>"Let's meet when I visit Japan. Krishna."</i>

00:21:39.540 --> 00:21:42.400
<i>"Good luck becoming a pro! Marcia."</i>

00:21:42.400 --> 00:21:44.080
<i>And Alex's is...</i>

00:21:44.080 --> 00:21:45.770
<i>"Baby steps"?</i>

00:21:45.770 --> 00:21:47.800
<i>A baby's steps?</i>

00:21:47.800 --> 00:21:49.760
<i>Does that mean toddling?</i>

00:21:49.760 --> 00:21:52.120
<i>That will turn into a giant stride?</i>

00:21:52.490 --> 00:21:57.620
<i>It guess it means small steps will eventually 
turn into one large step forward.</i>

00:21:57.620 --> 00:22:01.670
<i>I personally want to start with giant strides...</i>

00:22:01.670 --> 00:22:05.380
<i>Oh, yeah. Marcia said something like 
that to me on the first day, too...</i>

00:22:08.860 --> 00:22:11.390
Tear ducts collapsing

00:22:14.080 --> 00:22:15.370
<i>But it'll be okay.</i>

00:22:15.840 --> 00:22:17.500
<i>As long as we continue tennis.</i>

00:22:19.290 --> 00:22:21.230
<i>So everyone, do your best.</i>

00:22:21.880 --> 00:22:23.520
<i>I will, too.</i>

00:22:24.450 --> 00:22:27.780
<i>If we do our best, we'll meet again.</i>

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:25.020
Next Time

00:24:00.340 --> 00:24:03.440
Um, please play a match against me, Takuma-san!

00:24:03.440 --> 00:24:06.000
In order for me to go pro,

00:24:06.000 --> 00:24:08.270
I can't lose any more matches from now on.

00:24:08.270 --> 00:24:09.840
I have to show results.

00:24:10.090 --> 00:24:12.690
So I beg of you, just one match!

00:24:12.690 --> 00:24:13.600
I see.

00:24:13.600 --> 00:24:15.530
If that's the case, I'll play against you.

00:24:15.530 --> 00:24:20.870
Well, I just happen to be in 
the mood to crush you to pulp.

00:24:20.870 --> 00:24:22.780
Next time on <i>Baby Steps</i>,

00:24:21.700 --> 00:24:25.020
Takuma's Decision

00:24:22.780 --> 00:24:23.900
"Takuma's Decision."

00:24:25.210 --> 00:24:31.010
End
